# Exclusions for `docker build -f apps/normal-server/Dockerfile .`
#
# The name is not a typo. The build context is the *repository root* (a workspace package cannot be
# installed without its workspace), so a `.dockerignore` sitting in this directory would never be
# read. BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` first and falls back to `<context>/.dockerignore`,
# which is how a per-Dockerfile ignore list can live next to its Dockerfile instead of at the root.
#
# Everything below is either rebuilt inside the image, useless to it, or must not be in an image at
# all. The `node_modules` line is the one that matters most: copying a pnpm store into the context
# costs hundreds of megabytes and the platform-specific binaries in it are wrong for Alpine anyway.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Rebuilt in the builder stage.
dist
**/dist
release
**/release
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Repository furniture with no bearing on the image.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.superpowers
docs
deploy
requirement.txt
README.md
**/*.md

# Test and e2e artefacts.
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
test-results
apps/lite/e2e
apps/normal-server/test
apps/normal-server/.e2e
apps/normal-web/e2e
apps/normal-web/test

# Never: real secrets, local databases, local editor state.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
bind-poker.run.json
